@ seconds left, full? -> countdown of the account view, drawn into PICT
@ (OTP draws the per-second updates itself from TBLS; this is for full draws).
@ full: the whole bar (after a redraw); otherwise only the 3 px of the second
@ that just passed are erased.  The seconds are always 3 characters wide, so
@ they overwrite the previous value.  Allocates little: on a 48G with ~13 KB
@ free, every byte made each second brings the next garbage collection closer.
\<< \-> l f
  \<<
    IF f NOT THEN
      PICT { #2d #50d } #90d #4d BLANK REPL
      IF l 0 > THEN PICT { #2d #50d } l 3 * R\->B #4d BLANK NEG REPL END
    ELSE
      PICT l 3 * 2 + R\->B #50d 2 \->LIST f 3 * R\->B #4d BLANK REPL
    END
    PICT { #113d #48d } l 10 < " " "" IFTE l \->STR + "s" + 2 \->GROB REPL
  \>>
\>>
